# TypeScript Conventions

- `strict` mode; no implicit `any`. Avoid `any` — use `unknown` and narrow.
- Explicit return types on exported functions.
- Validate external input with Zod at boundaries; infer types from schemas.
- Keep the layering: `handler -> service -> repository/processor`. Services
  contain no AWS SDK calls; those live in repositories behind interfaces.
- Throw typed domain errors; never swallow errors silently.
- All code and comments in English.

```typescript
// BAD: swallowed error, AWS detail leaking into the service
try { await ddb.send(cmd); } catch (e) {}

// GOOD: repository wraps AWS, service stays clean, error is typed + logged
try {
  await documentRepository.create(doc);
} catch (cause) {
  logger.error("Failed to create document", { documentId: doc.id, cause });
  throw new DocumentPersistError(doc.id, { cause });
}
```
